    {
      "id": "7b8f154c-4221-4b83-8e23-937c58026701",
      "name": "Sticky Note ff8b0362",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -416,
        -496
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Reference · Full ticket triage (L1→L3)\nRyan's Day 3 deck (`workshop3.html`), slides:\n**32** L3 splits Reply, Risk and Context.\n**37** Add customer context with Data Tables\n**38** Stretch L3 — same tickets.\n**44** Export your Proof pack before you leave.\n\n**Goal:** Reference build of the whole day: ticket in, one orchestrator, three specialists, customer table, Switch to the trays. Use it to compare with your own.\n\n**Done when:** Three specialist roles produce a joint output with customer context and an explicit human gate.\n\nProof (slide 44): The Proof pack includes an export or screenshot, routing rules, a named human gate, and the level reached.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 380
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "675ee17d-cb40-4516-9fb3-742db377919a",
      "name": "Sticky Note e890b785",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        144,
        -496
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## IN · Ticket Input\nSlide 19: the shared fixture, same tickets all day.\nNow loaded: **WL-9002** (CUST-004) \"My card reader arrived broken. I would like a refund or a replacement.\"\nSwap the message to test WL-1027 (invoice copy) or WL-9002 (card reader).",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 260,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "21ca28ac-be59-4b9e-a3ca-e03177449a7d",
      "name": "Sticky Note 4496d85a",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        752,
        -496
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## AI Agent · the orchestrator\nSlides 23–25: model thinks, System Message guides, Tools act, Memory remembers.\n\n**System Message:** You are a support triage agent for a payment company. Read the ticket and decide its priority: - high: money was taken wrongly, payments do not work, or the customer threatens a …\n\nChat Model: n8n AI credits, no API key needed.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fd59ccaa-8056-4fab-aa2a-a67b5c32e3d8",
      "name": "Sticky Note fcd5dad1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1424,
        -496
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## THE TRAYS · Switch, Mode: Rules\nSlide 20: no AI here. It reads `{{ $json.output.priority }}` and picks the tray.\nRule order = output order: low → medium → high.\n\n`output.priority` comes from the Output Parser (slide 29). The agent gives the label, the Switch picks the route.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4deace56-9e5b-4a32-b0ae-fcc43d4afbf6",
      "name": "Sticky Note 687a15bc",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1648,
        928
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## OUT · human gate\nEach tray = one route. A grey branch means no item went there: that's fine.\nSlides 22 / 31: a person checks the tray before any customer gets a reply. No auto-send.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "73213983-bee4-4798-9d0c-b38164bc79dd",
      "name": "Sticky Note 61f9fb17",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        432,
        -496
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Simple Memory\nSlide 28: keeps the last messages of one session.\nTest: 'My favorite color is red' → 'What is my favorite color?'\nNew session = empty again.",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 300,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "7f94b465-2651-4ff5-8bff-c85163fa4878",
      "name": "Sticky Note 52bae13f",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1088,
        -496
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## THE FORM · Structured Output Parser\nSlides 29–30: fixed fields the agent must fill in.\n```\n{\"priority\": \"\", \"message\": \"\"}\n```\nThey land inside `output`, so the Switch reads `output.priority`.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "687b5794-9ead-460b-95b0-f6bacd9fcb11",
      "name": "Sticky Note 78d47b12",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        608,
        928
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Specialists · Tool slot of the AI Agent\nSlide 36: **Description chooses, System Message guides.** The question each specialist gets is written by the main agent (✨ Defined by agent).\n- **Customer Reply Agent:** Use this agent to write the reply to the customer. Give it the ticket message and the priority.\n- **Risk Agent:** Use this agent to assess ticket risk, urgency and whether escalation is required.\n- **Customer Context Agent:** Use this agent to look up the customer of the ticket by customer_id: customer type, transactions per hour, …",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 1020,
        "color": 2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ed407792-5e79-48f7-9b77-0b7a9f763e69",
      "name": "Sticky Note b86881da",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1184,
        672
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Data table tool · customer context\nSlide 37: looks up one row by `customer_id` (filled in by the agent).\nTable: **customer context**, 6 customers, 3 critical.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 300,
        "color": 4
      }
    }
